	abstract = {In the second of two posts on his paper ``How People Use ChatGPT'', written with a team of OpenAI researchers, David Deming describes what people use ChatGPT for, based on classifying users' messages with gpt-5. Non-work messages grew much faster than work messages between June 2024 and June 2025 and now make up 73\% of the total. The most common topics are practical guidance (28.3\%, including tutoring and teaching), writing (28.1\%, mostly editing or critiquing the user's own text and translation) and seeking information (21.3\%). Deming concludes that ChatGPT is practically useful and not currently on track to kill us all. – AI-generated abstract.},
