	langid = {english},
	abstract = {This essay is an adaptation of a talk I gave at the Human-Aligned AI Summer School 2019 about our work on mesa-optimisation. My goal here is to write an informal, accessible and intuitive introduction to the worry that we describe in our full-length report. I wish to draw a distinction which I think is crucial for clarity about AI alignment, yet is rarely drawn. That distinction is between the reward signal of a reinforcement learning (RL) agent and its ``utility function''. That is to say, it is not in general true that the policy of an RL agent is optimising for its reward.},
