	urldate = {2026-11-10},
	langid = {english},
	abstract = {Responding to Eliezer Yudkowsky's ``Death With Dignity'' post, Ladish grants for the sake of argument that humanity is very likely doomed because AI alignment is extremely hard and that the right goal is to maximize the log odds of survival, but questions whether ``dying with dignity'' is the right mindset for pursuing that goal, finding it demotivating and depressing. He proposes instead a framing borrowed from Magic: The Gathering, ``playing to your outs'': when you are far behind, minimizing losses almost always fails, so you should think ahead to the scenarios that would still give you a chance to win and plan for them, even if they are unlikely. He argues that this stance, playing carefully, choosing strategies with a shot at winning, and being ready to win if the opportunity arises, works for a wider variety of mental setups. – AI-generated abstract.},
