	abstract = {Flint shares tentative reflections, which he describes as still far too vague, on how to approach the task of aligning the systems that will most influence the future with what is actually good. He argues that we should seek to understand alignment rather than intelligence: intelligence matters only as one means by which systems exert influence over the future, so what we need to understand is how any system can exert such influence and how to align powerful systems with what is worth protecting. He further argues that we should align systems in general, not just AI: rather than debating whether AI will look like a singleton, a tool, cloud services or a society of competing entities, the unifying question is how to build things, including treaties, financial systems and tools, that are and remain consistently beneficial to all life. – AI-generated abstract.},
