	urldate = {2026-11-10},
	langid = {english},
	abstract = {Realizing that the world is in deep trouble does not oblige one to become ever more grim. Many people carry an internal grim-o-meter that they dutifully calibrate against the state of the world, growing grimmer with each piece of bad news, as a detective in a movie does while a kidnapped child is in danger. This is narrative thinking, and it is a terrible plan: a grim-o-meter with a dozen settings cannot be meaningfully connected to the state of a world of billions of people with astronomical future potential at stake. The author argues that one can deeply want the world to be different, draw on a well of cold resolve, and still be curious, playful and relaxed, and recommends detaching one's demeanor from the grimness of the world. – AI-generated abstract.},
