	langid = {english},
	abstract = {Many machine learning researchers claim to think there is a moderate chance that AI systems will destroy human civilization in the next few decades, yet they often display what Bryan Caplan has called a "missing mood": they do not seem upset, worried or sad about it, and do not seem to take any specific actions as a result. Elon Musk is an exception. When asked by Joe Rogan about his warnings on AI, Musk looks sad, dejected and fatalistic, and explains that he tried for years to convince people to slow down and regulate AI, without success, and that the usual slow process of regulation is not relevant to a technology that could be too dangerous to wait for. The author presents Musk's reaction as an example of a mood that fits the beliefs one claims to hold. – AI-generated abstract.},
