	urldate = {2026-11-10},
	langid = {english},
	abstract = {In her first few jobs, the author felt desperate to have an impact, and fear propelled her to action. Three factors formed a "desperation hamster wheel", a cycle of desperation, inadequacy and burnout that got her nowhere: a self-worth defined wholly by impact, a constant feeling of not being skilled or talented enough, and black-and-white thinking. This led her to think too narrowly about opportunities and about her skills, and to worse work habits and performance, in a vicious cycle. She now feels much better and able to approach impact with openness and curiosity, and offers guesses about what helped, including medication, changing roles to play to her strengths, grieving that she was not as good as she had hoped, and living more intentionally. – AI-generated abstract.},
